@startuml
title Spott - Fixed-Area Search, Departure Report and Occupancy Feedback
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 220
hide footbox
autonumber

actor "Reporting\nDriver" as Reporter
boundary "Reporter\nApp" as ReporterApp
control "Spott\nBackend" as Backend
database "Spott\nData" as Store
participant "Push\nService" as Push
boundary "Searcher\nApp" as SearcherApp
actor "Searching\nDriver" as Searcher
participant "Device Location\nService" as Location
participant "External\nNavigation" as Navigation

note over ReporterApp, SearcherApp
  Parking operations require authentication.
  The backend validates each write against current state and server time.
  Device suggestions always require explicit driver confirmation.
end note

== Start a search around a chosen point ==
Searcher -> SearcherApp : Choose fixed center, radius and filters
SearcherApp -> Backend : Start active search(center, radius, filters)
Backend -> Store : Save ACTIVE search and notification preference
Backend --> SearcherApp : Search active with the chosen circle
note over SearcherApp, Location
  Moving the phone does not move the search center.
  A new center or radius requires an explicit user action.
end note

== Publish an upcoming departure ==
Reporter -> ReporterApp : Confirm report at saved or selected position
ReporterApp -> Backend : Publish upcoming departure(position)
Backend -> Store : Create POTENTIALLY_LEAVING;\nexpiresAt = serverNow + upcomingTtl
Backend --> ReporterApp : Report id, status and expiry
Backend -> Store : Find ACTIVE searches whose saved circles\ncontain the report and whose filters match
Store --> Backend : Eligible recipients and current preferences
loop Each eligible search with push permission and opt-in
  Backend -> Backend : Recheck active search and unexpired report
  Backend -> Push : Nearby upcoming-departure alert
  Push -> SearcherApp : Deliver alert(report id and status)
  SearcherApp --> Searcher : Show that a spot may become available
end

== Driver decision or report timeout ==
alt Author confirms departure before expiry
  Reporter -> ReporterApp : Explicitly confirm departure
  ReporterApp -> Backend : Confirm departure(report id)
  Backend -> Store : Check author, upcoming state and expiry;\nset RECENTLY_VACATED and departureConfirmedAt;\nexpiresAt = serverNow + vacatedTtl
  Backend --> ReporterApp : Confirmed status and new expiry
  ref over Backend, SearcherApp
    Reuse fixed-area matching and permitted alert delivery
    for the recently-vacated update
  end ref
else Author cancels upcoming departure before expiry
  Reporter -> ReporterApp : Cancel upcoming departure
  ReporterApp -> Backend : Cancel report(report id)
  Backend -> Store : Check author and upcoming state; set CANCELLED
  Backend --> ReporterApp : Cancellation accepted
  Backend -> SearcherApp : Live report update: remove cancelled suggestion
else Report reaches expiresAt
  Backend -> Backend : Detect deadline using server time
  Backend -> Store : Set EXPIRED if status is still active
  Backend -> SearcherApp : Live report update: remove expired suggestion
end

== Inspect a still-active report ==
opt Selected report is active and unexpired
  Searcher -> SearcherApp : Open report details
  SearcherApp -> Backend : Read current report
  Backend -> Store : Read current state, expiry and verified zone rules
  Store --> Backend : Report, timestamps and reference data
  Backend --> SearcherApp : Details and heuristic confidence indicator
  opt Driver requests navigation
    Searcher -> SearcherApp : Navigate to selected report
    SearcherApp -> Navigation : Open destination coordinates
    Navigation --> SearcherApp : Handoff result
  end

  Searcher -> SearcherApp : Observe the spot and report "Occupied"
  SearcherApp -> Location : Request a fresh device position
  Location --> SearcherApp : Coordinates, timestamp and accuracy,\nor unavailable location
  SearcherApp -> Backend : Occupied feedback(report id, location evidence)
  Backend -> Store : Read latest report and proximity policy
  Store --> Backend : State, spot position, expiry and thresholds
  alt Active, unexpired report AND fresh, accurate, nearby evidence
    Backend -> Store : Atomically recheck conditions;\nrecord feedback and set OCCUPIED
    Backend --> SearcherApp : Occupied feedback accepted
    Backend -> ReporterApp : Live report update: OCCUPIED
    Backend -> Backend : Exclude report from new results and alerts
  else Evidence missing, stale, inaccurate, distant or report already closed
    Backend --> SearcherApp : Reject feedback with reason and current status
    note over Backend, Store : Rejected feedback does not change the report.
  end
end

== Stop active search ==
Searcher -> SearcherApp : Stop parking search
SearcherApp -> Backend : Stop search(search id)
Backend -> Store : Set search inactive
Backend --> SearcherApp : No new alerts generated for this search

note over Backend, SearcherApp
  Live queries exclude overdue reports even before expiry processing runs.
  Already dispatched alerts can arrive late; opening one rechecks the report.
  Timeout and proximity values are configurable, not fixed by this diagram.
end note
@enduml
